# 0026 XeMTL plugin: WindowServer surface marks, Tile4 scanout, page-off with compressed private copies
#
# Base:  plugin/ after 0005 + 0006 + 0007 (NvGfx xe 0.0.35)
# Files: plugin/NVMTLEventSync.m, plugin/NVMTLObjects.h, plugin/NVMTLObjects.m, plugin/XeMTLDevice.m,
#        plugin/nvmtl_vk.c, plugin/nvmtl_vk.h
# Apply: patch -p1 < patches/0026-plugin-marks-tile4-pageoff.patch
#
# Needs the 0024 accelerator (DRM client selectors 1-8; with an older one every feature below stays off).
#   - surface marks (§32.15): WindowServer's composites mark their surfaces pending at commit and ready when the GPU
#     finished, so the accel orders the flip after the composite and WindowServer itself never waits
#     (/private/tmp/xemtl-ws-nowait, recreated at boot by tools/e1); WindowServer's queue runs at HIGH GPU priority
#     (VK_KHR_global_priority) so an app's long batch cannot hold a composite
#   - Tile4 scanout (§32.16): scanout surfaces are drawn Tile4 when the accel turns it on and re-laid out in place
#     on the GPU when that changes
#   - page-off (§36.12, §37): WindowServer render targets (BGRA8, >= 1024x600, not scanout) are drawn into a private
#     optimal-tiling image -- Tile4 with ANV's CCS render compression (aux-map) -- instead of the linear pages.
#     After a composite the accel's device cache is made current; a CPU lock or a scan-out of the surface makes the
#     page-off thread copy the image back to the pages.  A surface paged off more than 4 times a second, or that
#     becomes a scanout surface, goes back to an image over its pages.
#   - coherence (§37.8): a surface keeps a private copy only while that copy is its one root texture in the process;
#     a later root that cannot share it sends it back to the pages first; a copy going away writes back under the
#     surface's sync and a new root waits for it.  A copy that lived < 2 s or was never drawn is not made again.
#   - defaults (§37.10): page-off on, copies made at once.  Off: /Library/GPUBundles/.xemtl-no-pageoff (or
#     /private/tmp/xemtl-no-pageoff until the next boot); promotion after 3 s / 100 commits instead:
#     /Library/GPUBundles/.xemtl-pageoff-lazy.  Experiments: /private/tmp/xemtl-noccs (INTEL_DEBUG=noccs),
#     /private/tmp/xemtl-pageoff-fastclear (clear never-written surfaces instead of uploading -- blanks screenshots).
#   - passtime (/tmp/nvmtl-passtime-request) logs per-pass GPU time, shader pair and draw count.
# Status: in daily use: screenshots correct, fps-probe 82-131 flips/s at 240 Hz, the Dock "genie" effect's busiest
# seconds 85-89 flips/s (60 before).
#
